## ❓ Essential Interview Questions

Q1: Why must the password policy be configured in the Default Domain Policy rather than a specific OU?
A1: Because password policies evaluate against the user object in the Active Directory database during the authentication phase, before the system checks which OU the user belongs to. It requires a single, domain-wide rule.

Q2: What is the purpose of the "Account Lockout Observation Window"?
A2: It determines how long the system remembers a bad password attempt. If the threshold is 5 attempts, and the observation window is 30 minutes, a user who fails 4 times, waits 31 minutes, and fails again will *not* be locked out, because the counter reset after 30 minutes.

Q3: A user is locked out and calls the IT Helpdesk. What tool do you use to unlock them?
A3: Active Directory Users and Computers (`dsa.msc`). Right-click the user -> Properties -> Account tab -> Check "Unlock account" and click Apply.